From 9920fdb5887c6ab45a56d5f9f4b356dd3ce0ebd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hsiu-Chi Tsai <hctsai@linux.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:15:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: scale the TXQ memory limit with RAM

mac80211 lets the TXQs of a radio hold up to 16 MiB with VHT and 4 MiB
without. On a board with 64 MiB of RAM that is about all the free memory,
and a wired-to-Wi-Fi flood can run it out of memory.

Cap the default limit of each wiphy at 1/32 of totalram_pages(), the
MemTotal of /proc/meminfo, so that two wiphys with the default limit stay
within 1/16 together. VHT radios keep 16 MiB from 512 MiB of MemTotal up,
and other radios keep 4 MiB from 128 MiB up. A limit the driver sets in
wiphy->txq_memory_limit still takes precedence.

Signed-off-by: Hsiu-Chi Tsai <hctsai@linux.com>
---
 net/mac80211/tx.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/net/mac80211/tx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/tx.c
@@ -1593,6 +1593,7 @@ int ieee80211_txq_setup_flows(struct iee
 	int i;
 	bool supp_vht = false;
 	enum nl80211_band band;
+	u64 limit;
 
 	ret = fq_init(fq, 4096);
 	if (ret)
@@ -1615,6 +1616,11 @@ int ieee80211_txq_setup_flows(struct iee
 	if (!supp_vht)
 		fq->memory_limit = 4 << 20; /* 4 Mbytes */
 
+	/* Keep the queues within 1/32 of RAM on small systems. */
+	limit = (u64)totalram_pages() * PAGE_SIZE / 32;
+	if (limit < fq->memory_limit)
+		fq->memory_limit = limit;
+
 	codel_params_init(&local->cparams);
 	local->cparams.interval = MS2TIME(100);
 	local->cparams.target = MS2TIME(20);
